schema: doc/v1
epic: E-DFLOW
wu: E-DFLOW.W12
changes:
  - path: docs/design-flow.html
    tier: T1
    action: added
    distills: "The staged design flow - its six stages, the per-stage artifact shapes, the closing lists, the close, the Tier-3 review and the build hand-over. Moved from docs/work/design-flow-base.html, not copied: the epic plan promised 'a new T1 process doc - the design flow, sibling to workflow.html' and it was never delivered, which is why the gate red on it. Fixed in the move: the doc-assets prefix for the new depth, and data-artifact='base-flow', a type verify-doc does not define."
  - path: docs/component-design.html
    tier: T1
    action: added
    distills: "The component-design contract - what a design file holds, its sections, the TSDoc it retires into. Moved from docs/work/component-design-base.html; its own meta line already read 'promotion decided at W4 distillation'. Its canonical-exemplar link pointed at components/header-table.html, a file W8 deleted, and now states the DEC-16 retirement contract it was illustrating. Its provenance line still hedged 'T3 until W4 validates... whether this becomes a T1 process doc is decided at that distillation' while the meta line already said T1 - the doc contradicted its own badge. Caught by this WU's own code review (altitude dimension) and now records what happened: promoted at W12, as its own doc rather than a section of the flow spec."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-13-onboarding-capabilities.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "The proxy-revert question, homed AND answered. It existed only in W11's result doc, which this WU archives - archiving it would have destroyed the sole copy of a real open question. Records what ships today (Onboarding.tsx renders 'Stop routing' inside the set-proxy step, gated on auto && state == done), what run #8 proposed, and why that reasoning is false against the code. The owner then took the call during this WU: the affordance stays, its gating already scopes it to this machine (canAutoSetup limits it to macOS/Windows, target == defaultProxyTarget excludes phone/Firefox/terminal runs), so the capability is unchanged and the record needed no amendment; the shipped assertion is inherited, not retired. Also records that inherited binds the capability and not the coordinates - run #8 moves the control into the step rail - and that two revert paths exist, the in-screen button and the quit-time Remove/Keep prompt, both invoking unset_proxy in setup.rs. One pre-existing broken link fixed in passing: setup.ts, a file that has never existed, is setup.rs."
  - path: docs/decisions/decisions-index.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "DEC-13's row records the proxy-revert call and links to it. The '1 open' badge it briefly carried came off when the owner answered within this same WU."
  - path: docs/design-rules/design-rules-index.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "'One component's contract' now names its TSDoc in ui/src/components/, not a registry design file in docs/work/. That is DEC-16's end state and KeyValueRow already demonstrates it - the old row pointed into T3 scratch this WU archives. Also repoints the flow-spec link to its new T1 path."
  - path: docs/backlog/roadmap.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "E-REPLAY carries design run #7's facts inline instead of linking to the run doc: the Field proposal and its warrant (KeyValueRow, Select and SourceSurface each refuse it in their own @avoid), and the three things the run leaves blocked on that epic - the replay API contract, whether an edited draft survives navigation, and Field's own design file. A run doc is T3 and cannot be a durable dependency."
  - path: docs/work-planning.html
    tier: T1
    action: updated
    distills: "The design-run row's link follows the flow spec to its T1 path, closing a T1 to T3 edge."
  - path: docs/decisions/dec-24-design-review-dimension.html
    tier: T2
    action: updated
    distills: "Both links follow the promoted specs to their T1 paths."
  - path: docs/work/2026-09-02-dflow-w12-plan.html
    tier: T3
    action: added
    distills: "The WU plan - the failure census measured from the gate rather than guessed, the distillation targets, and the open question on where the flow spec belongs."
  - path: docs/work/2026-09-02-dflow-w12-result.html
    tier: T3
    action: added
    distills: "The result report - outcome, the promotion the epic plan promised, what the sweep broke and what that proved, deviations, the nine seam verdicts with their evidence, distillation and follow-ups. Updated when the owner answered the DEC-13 question: it is no longer listed as work owed to the build WU, which now inherits the assertion and re-points it at the new host."
